WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:11.600
From China's perspective, Taiwan is essentially
a renegade province located roughly 100 miles

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.380
off of China's coast, a part of China that
has to be returned by force if necessary.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.619
From the U.S. perspective, however.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:24.160
While the United States government acknowledges
China's position that the Taiwan is a part

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.189
of China, it doesn't recognize or endorse
that position.

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:33.250
Taiwan doesn't have a seat in the United Nations,
and the vast majority of countries around

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:38.000
the world do not recognize Taiwan as a sovereign,
independent country.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.620
The reason for that is because countries cannot
have diplomatic relations with both China

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.620
and Taiwan.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.220
They essentially are forced to choose.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.820
Most countries, including the United States,
will choose to recognize the People's Republic

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:58.720
of China and instead only maintain unofficial
relations with Taiwan.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.940
Taiwan has a complex history marked by the
interplay of indigenous groups with colonial

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.409
powers from the Dutch to the Japanese.

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:10.439
After World War Two, the Chinese civil war
erupted, pitting Mao Zedong and the Chinese

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:13.159
Communist Party against Chiang Kai shek and
the nationalists.

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:19.460
In 1949, Chiang Kai shek and his followers
fled to the island of Taiwan while Mao established

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.950
the People's Republic of China on the mainland.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:28.049
Mao always sought to reclaim Taiwan and unify
that with the mainland.

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:32.549
While Chiang Kai shek essentially viewed his
government and his regime as a government

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:37.520
in exile, that would eventually take over
the mainland and unify it under his terms,

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.560
the Korean War really changed the dynamics.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.310
When President Truman made the decision to
send the U.S. Navy into the Taiwan Strait,

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:50.450
prevent Mao from opening another front while
the United States was fighting North Korea

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.030
in the Korean War.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:56.650
And that really locked in the lines that we
see today from the Chinese Communist Party's

00:01:56.650 --> 00:02:01.520
perspective, though, Taiwan is an unresolved
part of the Chinese civil war.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:08.440
It is a piece of territory that they view
as lost and that should be recovered by force

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.060
if necessary.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.150
Taiwan is a pluralistic society, a liberal
democracy.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:21.430
So saying what 23 million people want is quite
difficult.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:27.459
By public polling on Taiwan reveals that there
is virtually no support for unification with

00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:31.160
China, and there is growing support for independence.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:36.420
However, Taiwanese people are very pragmatic
and they understand that pursuing independence

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.490
is likely to prompt China to use force against
Taiwan to prevent that outcome.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:47.760
And therefore, most Taiwanese understand that
the status quo is probably the best that they

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.900
could hope for, at least for the time being.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:54.569
And the status quo, as they would define it,
is the Taiwan is a de facto independent country.

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:59.030
It has its own military, it has its own elected
government and currency.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.090
But at the same time it doesn't have a seat
in the United Nations.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:07.230
And most countries in the world do not recognize
it as an independent country.

